wider. And of course, that has some disadvantages, like it's hard for babies to pay attention or to concentrate. But, you know, one of the things I say is when we say that children are bad at paying attention. What we really mean is they're bad at not paying attention. So what they're bad at is filtering out all the other kinds of things that are going on around them, that fascinating little piece of dust on the floor or the sound of that airplane high up in the sky that we grownups don't even notice. They're bad at not paying attention to those things and just paying attention to the thing they're supposed to be paying attention to, like putting on their jacket to get to school. In recent years, you've become interested in the other end of the
