And it's sort of fascinating. It's been a wonderful learning experience for me. You know, if you talk to people in robotics, for instance, and you think, okay, well, this should be easy, right? You'll just show the robot that someone's reaching for something and it'll imitate. But it turns out what the robot will do is imitate exactly the absolute trajectory of what the person does. And then if you just move the object over an inch, it'll fail because it doesn't know what it's supposed to what it's supposed to do. Whereas the kids will figure out what is it that you want me to do? Is that the right kind of thing to do? What would be a better way of doing it? They're they're doing this in a much more sophisticated way.
